'''Jarek Yeager’s racer''' or '''Yeager's ship'''<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|yeagers-ship|Yeager's ship}}</ref> was a [[Racing starfighter|racer]] that belonged to [[Jarek Yeager]]. He had used it to compete in races on the ''[[Colossus]]'' platform, but by [[34 ABY]] Yeager no longer did so, keeping the ship in his private hangar in his [[Jarek Yeager's Repair Station|repair shop]].<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" /> Jarek continued to refuse to fly the racer, until the [[Platform Classic]]. Jarek again flew his racer in this race against his brother, [[Marcus Speedstar]].<ref name="The Platform Classic" />

Yeager would later fly this craft alongside [[Ace Squadron]] in defense of the ''Colossus'' during its [[Battle of Castilon|escape]] from [[First Order]] forces on [[Castilon]]. During the battle Yeager would down several [[TIE/fo space superiority fighter|TIE fighters]], allowing the ''Colossus'' to escape.<ref name="No Escape 2" />

In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="TROS Date">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']] to one [[Standard year|year]] after the events of [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. As ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of ''The Force Awakens'' to [[34 ABY]], the events of ''The Rise of Skywalker'' must occur in [[35 ABY]].</ref> Yeager flew<ref name="Fascinating Facts">''[[Star Wars: Fascinating Facts]]''</ref> the racer as part of a [[Citizens' Fleet|fleet]]<ref name="Bucket List The Escape">{{SW|url=news/buckets-list-extra-the-escape-part-2-star-wars-resistance|text=Bucket's List Extra: 5 Fun Facts from "The Escape - Part 2" - ''Star Wars Resistance''}}</ref> assembled by [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] to assist the Resistance during the [[Battle of Exegol|battle]] against the [[Sith Eternal military|Sith Eternal forces]] over the [[planet]] [[Exegol]].<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

{{Ship-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Originally designed for ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'', Yeager's ship was among the ships modeled by [[Industrial Light & Magic|ILM]] and included in the final battle of [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']].<ref name="Bucket List" />

